      "content_utf8": "L1 SYNTHETIC FIXTURE ONLY. This is an invented single-record store model, not a host operation.\nL2 Initial durable record is old-complete-value; proposed replacement is new-complete-value. There is one writer and no concurrent reader during publication.\nL3 The model guarantees atomic same-directory rename. Syncing a temporary record makes its complete bytes durable. Syncing the directory after rename makes the name replacement durable.\nL4 A crash before rename recovers old-complete-value. A crash after rename but before directory sync may recover either complete value. A crash after directory sync recovers new-complete-value.\nL5 Propose write-temporary, sync-temporary, rename-atomically, sync-directory, then acknowledge-success. Never acknowledge before directory sync. Recovery must never expose a partial value.\nL6 These are explicit abstract model assumptions, not portable filesystem guarantees. Unpublished temporary data can be discarded only in the model after preserving the authoritative record.\n",
      "sha256": "9695bacead928015e00990cae3cbfdcd3f232f667a5e73eb4344d9383add7a8a"
